{"formatVersion":1,"translationId":"BSB","textDirection":"ltr","bookId":"PHM","bookName":"Philemon","chapters":[{"number":1,"lastVerse":25,"verses":[{"number":1,"lines":[{"text":"Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother,"},{"text":"To Philemon our beloved fellow worker,"}]},{"number":2,"lines":[{"text":"to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:"}]},{"number":3,"lines":[{"text":"Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."}]},{"number":4,"lines":[{"text":"I always thank my God, remembering you in my prayers,"}]},{"number":5,"lines":[{"text":"because I hear about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints."}]},{"number":6,"lines":[{"text":"I pray that your partnership in the faith may become effective as you fully acknowledge every good thing that is ours in Christ."}]},{"number":7,"lines":[{"text":"I take great joy and encouragement in your love, because you, brother, have refreshed the hearts of the saints."}]},{"number":8,"lines":[{"text":"So although in Christ I am bold enough to order you to do what is proper,"}]},{"number":9,"lines":[{"text":"I prefer to appeal on the basis of love. For I, Paul, am now aged, and a prisoner of Christ Jesus as well."}]},{"number":10,"lines":[{"text":"I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains."}]},{"number":11,"lines":[{"text":"Formerly he was useless to you, but now he has become useful both to you and to me."}]},{"number":12,"lines":[{"text":"I am sending back to you him who is my very heart."}]},{"number":13,"lines":[{"text":"I would have liked to keep him with me, so that on your behalf he could minister to me in my chains for the gospel."}]},{"number":14,"lines":[{"text":"But I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness will not be out of compulsion, but by your own free will."}]},{"number":15,"lines":[{"text":"For perhaps this is why he was separated from you for a while, so that you might have him back for good—"}]},{"number":16,"lines":[{"text":"no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord."}]},{"number":17,"lines":[{"text":"So if you consider me a partner, receive him as you would receive me."}]},{"number":18,"lines":[{"text":"But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to my account."}]},{"number":19,"lines":[{"text":"I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it—not to mention that you owe me your very self."}]},{"number":20,"lines":[{"text":"Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in Christ."}]},{"number":21,"lines":[{"text":"Confident of your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even more than I ask."}]},{"number":22,"lines":[{"text":"In the meantime, prepare a guest room for me, because I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you."}]},{"number":23,"lines":[{"text":"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,"}]},{"number":24,"lines":[{"text":"as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers."}]},{"number":25,"lines":[{"text":"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit."}]}]}]}
